# The arithmetic masks: what a form wears to be added, subtracted, multiplied, divided and negated by the same words a
# number is (note/term/plan/decisions-2026-10.md, D5). A form that wears `addition` is added by `add`, written as it is
# for two numbers, and a task bounded by `need addition` adds whatever it is handed: the checker turns the operator on
# such a value into the mask's task (check/infer.ts `ARITHMETIC_MASKS`). `like self` is the form wearing the mask, so
# a big integer is added to a big integer and answers one.
#
# These replace the shelved code/mask/ files of the same names, written before masks had typed signatures.

mark stable

mask addition
  task add
    take self
    take other, like self
    like self

mask subtraction
  task subtract
    take self
    take other, like self
    like self

mask multiplication
  task multiply
    take self
    take other, like self
    like self

mask division
  task divide
    take self
    take other, like self
    like self

mask negation
  task negate
    take self
    like self
